\`\`\`

## Acceptance criteria

1. Rendering: the footer shows the badge at 36px high with the exact colors, radius, border and shadow above, in both light and dark site themes.
2. Hover: the "+" nudges and the shadow grows; the menu does not open on hover, with no layout shift.
3. Open/close: a click opens the bubbles above the badge (below near the top of the screen), inside the viewport; outside click, Escape and a second click close them.
4. Keyboard: Tab, Enter/Space, arrows, Home/End and Escape work as specified, focus returns to the badge, and the focus ring is visible.
5. Reduced motion: with prefers-reduced-motion enabled, nothing moves; changes are instant or fades.
"
`;

exports[`generatePrompt > snapshot: bubbles-8 1`] = `
"# Add a "Made by" signature badge to this project

## Goal

Add this signature badge to the footer of the current project, using the project's own stack and conventions (components, styling approach, file structure). The badge reads "Crafted by Eight Links".
Match the visual spec and behavior below exactly. The reference implementation at the end is the source of truth: adapt it to the project rather than pasting it as-is when a native approach fits better. Add no new dependency.

## Visual spec

- Layout: Pill. [avatar] · normal text · bold text · icon, in one row, vertically centered, no wrapping.
- Order: normal text, then bold text. One regular space between them.
- Normal text: "Crafted by", weight 400.
- Bold text: "Eight Links", weight 500.
- Font: system stack only, no web font: -apple-system,system-ui,"SF Pro Text","Helvetica Neue","Segoe UI",Roboto,sans-serif.
- Size S: height 30px, font size 13px, padding 0 10px 0 4px, gap 6px.
- Corner radius: 4.5px.
- Border: none.
- Shadow: none.
- Icon: a "+" (two 2px strokes, round caps), 12px, in the icon color. It rotates 45° into "×" while the menu is open.
- Avatar: round, 22px, background #FF6B35, initials "EL" in #000000, weight 600, 9px.
- Colors follow the site theme through prefers-color-scheme.
- Light palette:
  - Background: #14141C
  - Border: #2E2E3A
  - Normal text: #8A8A99
  - Bold text: #FFFFFF
  - Icon: #8A8A99
  - Backdrop blur: none
- Dark palette:
  - Background: #14141C
  - Border: #2E2E3A
  - Normal text: #8A8A99
  - Bold text: #FFFFFF
  - Icon: #8A8A99
  - Backdrop blur: none
- Scope every class with a unique prefix and reset box-sizing, margin, padding, font, line-height and list-style on the badge and its children, so the host page CSS cannot leak in.

## Behavior

- Motion uses springs, expressed in CSS as linear() easings (values in the reference): fast = 0.08s, no bounce; moderate = 0.16s, no bounce; slow = 0.24s, bounce 0.12; slow exit = 0.16s tween. Never hard-code other durations.
- Mode: Bubbles. Clicking the badge toggles a small menu of links ("bubbles"). Hovering does not open it.
- Links, in this order:
  1. X: https://x.com/eight
  2. GitHub: https://github.com/eight
  3. LinkedIn: https://linkedin.com/in/eight
  4. Dribbble: https://dribbble.com/eight
  5. YouTube: https://youtube.com/@eight
  6. Bluesky: https://bsky.app/profile/eight
  7. Email: mailto:eight@example.com
  8. Portfolio: https://eight.example
- Links open in the same tab.
- Bubbles: circles of 36px that become capsules with icon + label (label in the bold text color); same background, border and shadow as the badge; corner radius scaled like the badge; inline SVG icon 18px in the icon color. Touch target at least 44 × 44px.
- Labels are always visible.
- Placement: one row centered on the badge, 12px above it, 8px between bubbles, in a gentle arc (the middle sits 8px higher than the ends).
- If there is less room above than the menu height + 16px, open below with the arc inverted.
- Keep the row at least 8px from the viewport edges. If it is wider than the viewport minus 16px, use 2 rows, the longer one nearest the badge.
- Reposition on scroll and resize (requestAnimationFrame); close if the badge leaves the viewport.
- Opening: each bubble travels from the badge center to its place, scale 0.6 → 1, opacity 0 → 1 (slow spring), staggered 30ms from the center outwards. Closing: all together, back into the badge with a fade (slow exit). Bubble hover: scale 1.08 (fast).
- Use the native popover API (<ul popover="auto"> + popovertarget on the button) so the menu renders in the top layer: never clipped by overflow: hidden or a transform. Fall back to a class toggle + outside click + Escape where popover is unsupported. Without JS the popover opens centered and stays usable.
- Hide the menu when printing.
- On appear: the badge gives a short horizontal shake (±3px). Animate a wrapper, not the clickable element, so the hover effect never restarts it.
- On delay: every 5s, starting 5s after load, the badge shows a light sheen sweeping once from left to right across it (a gradient band on a clipped ::after). Loop it with CSS (one keyframe cycle per period), no timers.
- On hover: the badge scales to 1.04 (fast spring).
- prefers-reduced-motion: reduce → no movement, rotation or scaling; state changes are instant or fade only.

## Accessibility

- Disclosure pattern, not role="menu": the badge is a <button> named "Crafted by Eight Links, show links" with aria-expanded and aria-controls; the bubbles are a <ul> of <a>.
- Each bubble is named "{Channel}, opens in a new tab" (email: "Email {bold text}").
- Keyboard: Tab reaches the badge; Enter/Space opens and focuses the first bubble; arrow keys move between bubbles and wrap; Home/End jump to the first/last; Enter follows the link; Escape closes and returns focus to the badge; Tab from a bubble closes the menu and continues the tab order.
- Touch: tap to open, tap a bubble to navigate, tap outside to close.
- Visible focus: a 2px outline in the bold text color, offset 2px, on :focus-visible.
- The avatar and icons are decorative (alt="" / aria-hidden).
- Touch targets of at least 44 × 44px.

## Reference implementation

Standalone HTML/CSS/JS, tested in Chrome, Safari and Firefox:

\`\`\`html
<!-- Stampit badge · edit: https://stampit.example/create#c=abc -->
<style>.sp-test1234{--sp-test1234-fast:linear(0,.08,.24,.409,.558,.678,.77,.838,.887,.922,.947,.964,.976,.984,.989,.993,.995,.997,.998,.999,1);--sp-test1234-attention:cubic-bezier(.4,0,.2,1);--sp-test1234-repeat:linear;--sp-test1234-moderate:linear(0,.08,.238,.406,.554,.674,.767,.835,.885,.921,.946,.963,.975,.983,.989,.993,.995,.997,.998,.999,1);--sp-test1234-slow-exit:cubic-bezier(.4,0,1,1);--sp-test1234-slow:linear(0,.072,.224,.394,.551,.682,.784,.86,.913,.949,.973,.987,.996,1,1.002,1.003,1.003,1.003,1.002,1.002,1)}.sp-test1234,.sp-test1234 *,.sp-test1234 *::before,.sp-test1234 *::after{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0;border:0;font:inherit;line-height:inherit;letter-spacing:normal;text-transform:none;text-decoration:none;list-style:none;background:none;color:inherit;max-width:none;min-width:0;float:none}.sp-test1234{--sp-test1234-bg:#14141c;--sp-test1234-bd:#2e2e3a;--sp-test1234-tn:#8a8a99;--sp-test1234-tb:#ffffff;--sp-test1234-ic:#8a8a99;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;position:relative;vertical-align:middle;font-family:-apple-system,system-ui,"SF Pro Text","Helvetica Neue","Segoe UI",Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;line-height:1.2;text-align:left;white-space:nowrap;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;-moz-osx-font-smoothing:grayscale}.sp-test1234__pill{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;height:30px;padding:0 10px 0 4px;border-radius:4.5px;background:var(--sp-test1234-bg);box-shadow:none;color:var(--sp-test1234-tb);white-space:nowrap;cursor:pointer;user-select:none;-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent;outline:none;transition:transform .08s var(--sp-test1234-fast)}@keyframes sp-test1234-in{0%,100%{transform:none}20%,60%{transform:translateX(-3px)}40%,80%{transform:translateX(3px)}}@keyframes sp-test1234-rp{0%{transform:translateX(-110%)}18%,100%{transform:translateX(110%)}}.sp-test1234{animation:sp-test1234-in .48s var(--sp-test1234-attention) backwards}.sp-test1234__pill{position:relative;overflow:hidden}.sp-test1234__pill::after{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;border-radius:inherit;pointer-events:none;background:linear-gradient(105deg,transparent 30%,rgba(255,255,255,.55) 50%,transparent 70%);transform:translateX(110%);animation:sp-test1234-rp 5s var(--sp-test1234-repeat) 5s infinite}.sp-test1234__pill:hover{transform:scale(1.04)}.sp-test1234__pill:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--sp-test1234-tb);outline-offset:2px}.sp-test1234__pill{-webkit-appearance:none;appearance:none;text-align:left}.sp-test1234__av{flex:none;display:grid;place-items:center;width:22px;height:22px;border-radius:0.5px;overflow:hidden;background:#ff6b35;color:#000000;font-size:9px;font-weight:600;line-height:1}.sp-test1234__n{color:var(--sp-test1234-tn)}.sp-test1234__b{color:var(--sp-test1234-tb);font-weight:500}.sp-test1234__ic{flex:none;display:block;color:var(--sp-test1234-ic);transition:transform .16s var(--sp-test1234-moderate)}.sp-test1234__pill:hover .sp-test1234__ic{transform:rotate(15deg)}.sp-test1234__pill[aria-expanded=true] .sp-test1234__ic{transform:rotate(45deg)}.sp-test1234__menu{display:none;position:fixed;inset:0;width:fit-content;height:fit-content;max-width:calc(100vw - 16px);margin:auto;padding:8px;overflow:visible;background:none;border:0;color:inherit;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center;gap:8px;transition:display .16s allow-discrete,overlay .16s allow-discrete}.sp-test1234__menu:popover-open{display:flex}.sp-test1234__menu.is-open{display:flex}.sp-test1234__menu li{position:relative;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center}.sp-test1234[data-js] .sp-test1234__menu{width:auto;height:auto;max-width:none;margin:0;padding:0;pointer-events:none}.sp-test1234[data-js] .sp-test1234__menu li{position:absolute;pointer-events:auto;opacity:0;transform:translate(var(--dx,0),var(--dy,0)) scale(.6);transition:transform .16s var(--sp-test1234-slow-exit),opacity .16s var(--sp-test1234-slow-exit)}.sp-test1234[data-js] .sp-test1234__menu[data-open] li{opacity:1;transform:none;transition:transform .24s var(--sp-test1234-slow) var(--d,0s),opacity .24s var(--sp-test1234-slow) var(--d,0s)}.sp-test1234__bub{position:relative;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:4px;min-width:36px;height:36px;padding:0 12px 0 10px;border-radius:5.4px;background:var(--sp-test1234-bg);box-shadow:none;color:var(--sp-test1234-ic);white-space:nowrap;outline:none;-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent;transition:transform .08s var(--sp-test1234-fast)}.sp-test1234__bub::before{content:"";position:absolute;inset:-4px}.sp-test1234__bub:hover{transform:scale(1.08)}.sp-test1234__bub:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--sp-test1234-tb);outline-offset:2px}.sp-test1234__bub svg{display:block;flex:none;width:18px;height:18px}.sp-test1234__lb{color:var(--sp-test1234-tb);font-size:12px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){.sp-test1234{--sp-test1234-bg:#14141c;--sp-test1234-bd:#2e2e3a;--sp-test1234-tn:#8a8a99;--sp-test1234-tb:#ffffff;--sp-test1234-ic:#8a8a99}}@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.sp-test1234__ic{transition:none}.sp-test1234,.sp-test1234 .sp-test1234__pill,.sp-test1234 .sp-test1234__pill:hover{animation:none;transform:none}.sp-test1234 .sp-test1234__pill::after{animation:none;opacity:0}.sp-test1234 .sp-test1234__pill[aria-expanded=false]:hover .sp-test1234__ic{transform:none}.sp-test1234[data-js] .sp-test1234__menu li,.sp-test1234[data-js] .sp-test1234__menu[data-open] li{transform:none;transition-property:opacity;transition-delay:0s}.sp-test1234 .sp-test1234__bub,.sp-test1234 .sp-test1234__bub:hover{transform:none;transition:none}}@media print{.sp-test1234__menu{display:none}}</style>
