## Acceptance criteria

1. Rendering: the footer shows the badge at 30px high with the exact colors, radius, border and shadow above, in both light and dark site themes.
2. Hover: the "+" nudges and the shadow grows; the menu does not open on hover, with no layout shift.
3. Open/close: a click opens the bubbles above the badge (below near the top of the screen), inside the viewport; outside click, Escape and a second click close them.
4. Keyboard: Tab, Enter/Space, arrows, Home/End and Escape work as specified, focus returns to the badge, and the focus ring is visible.
5. Reduced motion: with prefers-reduced-motion enabled, nothing moves; changes are instant or fades.
"
`;

exports[`generatePrompt > snapshot: glass 1`] = `
"# Add a "Made by" signature badge to this project

## Goal

Add this signature badge to the footer of the current project, using the project's own stack and conventions (components, styling approach, file structure). The badge reads "Glassworks".
Match the visual spec and behavior below exactly. The reference implementation at the end is the source of truth: adapt it to the project rather than pasting it as-is when a native approach fits better. Add no new dependency.

## Visual spec

- Layout: Pill. [avatar] · normal text · bold text · icon, in one row, vertically centered, no wrapping.
- Order: bold text, then normal text. One regular space between them.
- Normal text: "(none)", weight 400.
- Bold text: "Glassworks", weight 500.
- Font: system stack only, no web font: ui-monospace,"SF Mono",Menlo,Consolas,monospace.
- Size S: height 30px, font size 13px, padding 0 10px 0 10px, gap 6px.
- Corner radius: 15px (a full capsule).
- Border: none.
- Shadow: none.
- Icon: an "arrow-up-right" (Lucide path: line 7,17 → 17,7 and polyline 7,7 17,7 17,17), 12px, 2px stroke, currentColor, in the icon color, aria-hidden (exact SVG in the reference).
- Avatar: none. Left and right padding are equal.
- Colors follow the site theme through prefers-color-scheme.
- Light palette:
  - Background: #FFFFFF14
  - Border: #FFFFFF29
  - Normal text: #FFFFFF99
  - Bold text: #FFFFFF
  - Icon: #FFFFFF99
  - Backdrop blur: 12px (backdrop-filter, with -webkit- prefix)
- Dark palette:
  - Background: #14141C
  - Border: #2E2E3A
  - Normal text: #8A8A99
  - Bold text: #FFFFFF
  - Icon: #8A8A99
  - Backdrop blur: none
- Scope every class with a unique prefix and reset box-sizing, margin, padding, font, line-height and list-style on the badge and its children, so the host page CSS cannot leak in.

## Behavior

- Motion uses springs, expressed in CSS as linear() easings (values in the reference): fast = 0.08s, no bounce; moderate = 0.16s, no bounce; slow = 0.24s, bounce 0.12; slow exit = 0.16s tween. Never hard-code other durations.
- Mode: Link. The whole badge is one <a href="https://glass.example"> opening in a new tab (target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer").
- Hover and keyboard focus: the arrow slides 2px up and 2px right (fast spring).
- On appear: the badge gives a short horizontal shake (±3px). Animate a wrapper, not the clickable element, so the hover effect never restarts it.
- On delay: every 5s, starting 5s after load, the badge shows a light sheen sweeping once from left to right across it (a gradient band on a clipped ::after). Loop it with CSS (one keyframe cycle per period), no timers.
- On hover: the badge scales to 1.04 (fast spring).
- prefers-reduced-motion: reduce → no movement, rotation or scaling; state changes are instant or fade only.

## Accessibility

- The link's accessible name is "Glassworks, opens in a new tab".
- Visible focus: a 2px outline in the bold text color, offset 2px, on :focus-visible.
- The avatar and icons are decorative (alt="" / aria-hidden).
- Touch targets of at least 44 × 44px.

## Reference implementation

Standalone HTML/CSS, tested in Chrome, Safari and Firefox:

\`\`\`html
<!-- Stampit badge · edit: https://stampit.example/create#c=abc -->
<style>.sp-test1234{--sp-test1234-fast:linear(0,.08,.24,.409,.558,.678,.77,.838,.887,.922,.947,.964,.976,.984,.989,.993,.995,.997,.998,.999,1);--sp-test1234-attention:cubic-bezier(.4,0,.2,1);--sp-test1234-repeat:linear}.sp-test1234,.sp-test1234 *,.sp-test1234 *::before,.sp-test1234 *::after{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0;border:0;font:inherit;line-height:inherit;letter-spacing:normal;text-transform:none;text-decoration:none;list-style:none;background:none;color:inherit;max-width:none;min-width:0;float:none}.sp-test1234{--sp-test1234-bg:#ffffff14;--sp-test1234-bd:#ffffff29;--sp-test1234-tn:#ffffff99;--sp-test1234-tb:#ffffff;--sp-test1234-ic:#ffffff99;--sp-test1234-blur:12px;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;position:relative;vertical-align:middle;font-family:ui-monospace,"SF Mono",Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:13px;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;line-height:1.2;text-align:left;white-space:nowrap;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;-moz-osx-font-smoothing:grayscale}.sp-test1234__pill{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;height:30px;padding:0 10px 0 10px;border-radius:15px;background:var(--sp-test1234-bg);box-shadow:none;color:var(--sp-test1234-tb);white-space:nowrap;cursor:pointer;user-select:none;-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent;outline:none;-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(var(--sp-test1234-blur));backdrop-filter:blur(var(--sp-test1234-blur));transition:transform .08s var(--sp-test1234-fast)}@keyframes sp-test1234-in{0%,100%{transform:none}20%,60%{transform:translateX(-3px)}40%,80%{transform:translateX(3px)}}@keyframes sp-test1234-rp{0%{transform:translateX(-110%)}18%,100%{transform:translateX(110%)}}.sp-test1234{animation:sp-test1234-in .48s var(--sp-test1234-attention) backwards}.sp-test1234__pill{position:relative;overflow:hidden}.sp-test1234__pill::after{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;border-radius:inherit;pointer-events:none;background:linear-gradient(105deg,transparent 30%,rgba(255,255,255,.55) 50%,transparent 70%);transform:translateX(110%);animation:sp-test1234-rp 5s var(--sp-test1234-repeat) 5s infinite}.sp-test1234__pill:hover{transform:scale(1.04)}.sp-test1234__pill:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--sp-test1234-tb);outline-offset:2px}.sp-test1234__n{color:var(--sp-test1234-tn)}.sp-test1234__b{color:var(--sp-test1234-tb);font-weight:500}.sp-test1234__ic{flex:none;display:block;color:var(--sp-test1234-ic);transition:transform .08s var(--sp-test1234-fast)}.sp-test1234__pill:hover .sp-test1234__ic,.sp-test1234__pill:focus-visible .sp-test1234__ic{transform:translate(2px,-2px)}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){.sp-test1234{--sp-test1234-bg:#14141c;--sp-test1234-bd:#2e2e3a;--sp-test1234-tn:#8a8a99;--sp-test1234-tb:#ffffff;--sp-test1234-ic:#8a8a99;--sp-test1234-blur:0px}}@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.sp-test1234__ic{transition:none}.sp-test1234,.sp-test1234 .sp-test1234__pill,.sp-test1234 .sp-test1234__pill:hover{animation:none;transform:none}.sp-test1234 .sp-test1234__pill::after{animation:none;opacity:0}.sp-test1234 .sp-test1234__pill:hover .sp-test1234__ic,.sp-test1234 .sp-test1234__pill:focus-visible .sp-test1234__ic{transform:none}}</style>
<div class="sp-test1234">
  <a class="sp-test1234__pill" href="https://glass.example" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Glassworks, opens in a new tab">
    <span><span class="sp-test1234__b">Glassworks</span></span>
    <svg class="sp-test1234__ic" width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="7" y1="17" x2="17" y2="7"/><polyline points="7 7 17 7 17 17"/></svg>
  </a>
</div>
\`\`\`

## Acceptance criteria

1. Rendering: the footer shows the badge at 30px high with the exact colors, radius, border and shadow above, in both light and dark site themes.
2. Hover: the arrow slides 2px up-right and the shadow grows, with no layout shift.
3. Click: the badge opens https://glass.example in a new tab.
4. Keyboard: Tab reaches the badge, the focus ring is visible, Enter follows the link.
5. Reduced motion: with prefers-reduced-motion enabled, nothing moves; changes are instant or fades.
"
`;

exports[`generatePrompt > snapshot: layout-card 1`] = `
"# Add a "Made by" signature badge to this project

## Goal

Add this signature badge to the footer of the current project, using the project's own stack and conventions (components, styling approach, file structure). The badge reads "Crafted by Ada Lovelace".
Match the visual spec and behavior below exactly. The reference implementation at the end is the source of truth: adapt it to the project rather than pasting it as-is when a native approach fits better. Add no new dependency.

## Visual spec

- Layout: Card. A small card: avatar 44px on the left; normal text (12px), bold text (16px) and the role (13px, normal text color) stacked on the right; the icon in the top-right corner; the social links always visible in a row underneath. The whole card is the link (a stretched ::before), the social links sit above it.
- Order: normal text, then bold text. One regular space between them.
- Normal text: "Crafted by", weight 400.
- Bold text: "Ada Lovelace", weight 500.
- Font: system stack only, no web font: -apple-system,system-ui,"SF Pro Text","Helvetica Neue","Segoe UI",Roboto,sans-serif.
- Size M: height 36px, font size 15px, padding 0 12px 0 4px, gap 8px.
- Corner radius: 18px (a full capsule).
- Border: none.
- Shadow: 0 1px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.08); on hover 0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.12).
- Icon: an "arrow-up-right" (Lucide path: line 7,17 → 17,7 and polyline 7,7 17,7 17,17), 14px, 2px stroke, currentColor, in the icon color, aria-hidden (exact SVG in the reference).
- Avatar: round, 28px, background #FF6B35, initials "AL" in #000000, weight 600, 11px.
- Colors follow the site theme through prefers-color-scheme.
- Light palette:
  - Background: #FFFFFF
  - Border: #0000000D
  - Normal text: #6E6E73
  - Bold text: #000000
  - Icon: #6E6E73
  - Backdrop blur: none
- Dark palette:
  - Background: #14141C
  - Border: #2E2E3A
  - Normal text: #8A8A99
  - Bold text: #FFFFFF
  - Icon: #8A8A99
  - Backdrop blur: none
- Scope every class with a unique prefix and reset box-sizing, margin, padding, font, line-height and list-style on the badge and its children, so the host page CSS cannot leak in.

## Behavior

- Motion uses springs, expressed in CSS as linear() easings (values in the reference): fast = 0.08s, no bounce; moderate = 0.16s, no bounce; slow = 0.24s, bounce 0.12; slow exit = 0.16s tween. Never hard-code other durations.
- Mode: Link. The whole badge is one <a href="https://ada.dev"> opening in a new tab (target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer").
- Hover and keyboard focus: the arrow slides 2px up and 2px right (fast spring).
- Hover: the shadow grows as specified (fast spring).
- Social links: 1 round icon link right of the badge, 6px apart, in this order:
  1. GitHub: https://github.com/ada
  Each is a 36px square with the badge's background, border, shadow and corner radius, the network logo in the icon color. They sit outside the layout (absolutely positioned right of the badge) and stay hidden until the badge is hovered or focused: then they slide in from 6px left and scale 0.8 → 1 with a fade (slow spring), 30ms apart, left to right, and leave together (slow exit). Always visible on touch screens (hover: none). Hovering one scales it to 1.06 (fast spring). Accessible name "{Network}, opens in a new tab".
- On appear: the badge gives a short horizontal shake (±3px). Animate a wrapper, not the clickable element, so the hover effect never restarts it.
- On delay: every 5s, starting 5s after load, the badge shows a light sheen sweeping once from left to right across it (a gradient band on a clipped ::after). Loop it with CSS (one keyframe cycle per period), no timers.
- On hover: the badge scales to 1.04 (fast spring).
- prefers-reduced-motion: reduce → no movement, rotation or scaling; state changes are instant or fade only.

## Accessibility

- The link's accessible name is "Crafted by Ada Lovelace, opens in a new tab".
- Visible focus: a 2px outline in the bold text color, offset 2px, on :focus-visible.
- The avatar and icons are decorative (alt="" / aria-hidden).
- Touch targets of at least 44 × 44px.

## Reference implementation

Standalone HTML/CSS, tested in Chrome, Safari and Firefox:

\`\`\`html
<!-- Stampit badge · edit: https://stampit.example/create#c=abc -->
