"# Add a "Made by" signature badge to this project

## Goal

Add this signature badge to the footer of the current project, using the project's own stack and conventions (components, styling approach, file structure). The badge reads "Crafted by Ada Lovelace".
Match the visual spec and behavior below exactly. The reference implementation at the end is the source of truth: adapt it to the project rather than pasting it as-is when a native approach fits better. Add no new dependency.

## Visual spec

- Layout: Stamp. A circle with the avatar in its center and the full text, upper-case, running around the edge (SVG textPath with textLength = the circumference). The text ring turns slowly (one turn per 24s, linear); no rotation with reduced motion.
- Order: normal text, then bold text. One regular space between them.
- Normal text: "Crafted by", weight 400.
- Bold text: "Ada Lovelace", weight 500.
- Font: system stack only, no web font: -apple-system,system-ui,"SF Pro Text","Helvetica Neue","Segoe UI",Roboto,sans-serif.
- Size M: height 36px, font size 15px, padding 0 12px 0 4px, gap 8px.
- Corner radius: 18px (a full capsule).
- Border: none.
- Shadow: 0 1px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.08); on hover 0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.12).
- Icon: an "arrow-up-right" (Lucide path: line 7,17 → 17,7 and polyline 7,7 17,7 17,17), 14px, 2px stroke, currentColor, in the icon color, aria-hidden (exact SVG in the reference).
- Avatar: round, 28px, background #FF6B35, initials "AL" in #000000, weight 600, 11px.
- Colors follow the site theme through prefers-color-scheme.
- Light palette:
  - Background: #FFFFFF
  - Border: #0000000D
  - Normal text: #6E6E73
  - Bold text: #000000
  - Icon: #6E6E73
  - Backdrop blur: none
- Dark palette:
  - Background: #14141C
  - Border: #2E2E3A
  - Normal text: #8A8A99
  - Bold text: #FFFFFF
  - Icon: #8A8A99
  - Backdrop blur: none
- Scope every class with a unique prefix and reset box-sizing, margin, padding, font, line-height and list-style on the badge and its children, so the host page CSS cannot leak in.

## Behavior

- Motion uses springs, expressed in CSS as linear() easings (values in the reference): fast = 0.08s, no bounce; moderate = 0.16s, no bounce; slow = 0.24s, bounce 0.12; slow exit = 0.16s tween. Never hard-code other durations.
- Mode: Link. The whole badge is one <a href="https://ada.dev"> opening in a new tab (target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer").
- Hover and keyboard focus: the arrow slides 2px up and 2px right (fast spring).
- Hover: the shadow grows as specified (fast spring).
- Social links: 1 round icon link right of the badge, 6px apart, in this order:
  1. GitHub: https://github.com/ada
  Each is a 36px square with the badge's background, border, shadow and corner radius, the network logo in the icon color. They sit outside the layout (absolutely positioned right of the badge) and stay hidden until the badge is hovered or focused: then they slide in from 6px left and scale 0.8 → 1 with a fade (slow spring), 30ms apart, left to right, and leave together (slow exit). Always visible on touch screens (hover: none). Hovering one scales it to 1.06 (fast spring). Accessible name "{Network}, opens in a new tab".
- On appear: the badge gives a short horizontal shake (±3px). Animate a wrapper, not the clickable element, so the hover effect never restarts it.
- On delay: every 5s, starting 5s after load, the badge shows a light sheen sweeping once from left to right across it (a gradient band on a clipped ::after). Loop it with CSS (one keyframe cycle per period), no timers.
- On hover: the badge scales to 1.04 (fast spring).
- prefers-reduced-motion: reduce → no movement, rotation or scaling; state changes are instant or fade only.

## Accessibility

- The link's accessible name is "Crafted by Ada Lovelace, opens in a new tab".
- Visible focus: a 2px outline in the bold text color, offset 2px, on :focus-visible.
- The avatar and icons are decorative (alt="" / aria-hidden).
- Touch targets of at least 44 × 44px.

